 "descriptive cells (owner, 2026-10-28, D2-2)": {
  "rule": "a cell is DESCRIPTIVE when its path is not naive and some active expert holds more than BLOCK_M rows at vLLM's default config for its T (r3_decode.geometry multi_tile_experts > 0): v4d's G 1 schedule gives that expert a second M-tile whose CTAs re-read its weight slab from DRAM (sigma 1, decodeC-cal scorer ambiguity 4). Computed from the registered pages' counts and that rule alone, before any decode page",
  "out of": "the CAL fit (v4d.fit_constants), the rho selection (sub-wave rms), E1-CAL-IN-SAMPLE, the replicate's E1 row, the rivals' CAL training rows (line, OLS), blind E1-DEC pooled and per model, the certification and the rival exclusions, and the replicate's sigma_page and the tightened blind bars (owner, 2026-10-28, review m3: from the kept cells' pairs only; the every-cell figure printed beside, DESCRIPTIVE)",
  "kept in": "G3-D shuffle and label (each pair holds the same counts or the same multiset on both sides, so the re-read cancels in d_us; G3-D label's MIN-T64 against L-T64-A<k> pair stays as registered), G3-D fill (BALANCED cells only; no DESCRIPTIVE cell is BALANCED), GD2, GD3 (instrument readings, no model in them), V-ALIGN, GD5, COPIES and G1 (a DESCRIPTIVE cell's refusal is still a STOP: the decode rules are not vLLM's)",
