 "SIGMA-D (DESCRIPTIVE)": {
  "rows": "per valid NATIVE DESCRIPTIVE main cell (CAL at the amended fit's constants and rho, blind at the finalised ones): the measured time, v4d's sigma-1 price, the L2-served estimate, e of each (dcommon.e_dec), served / sigma-1, and position = (v4d - meas) / (v4d - served) (0 at sigma 1, 1 at the served estimate); per model the C5.stats of both e and the median position",
  "L2-served estimate": "v4d's price of the same cell with every CTA of an expert's second or later M-tile reading no weight slab (its slab served from L2 at zero DRAM bytes; its activation share kept), everything else v4d's unchanged: the same live CTAs and launch order at G 1, the floor, the partial-wave tail under CORES, rho, the dead term, B_other and the constants (d2common.served_price: r3_timing_model.window's G 1 reads, slab removed where pid_m // npn is not the expert's first M-tile)",
  "never": "fitted, selected, a bar, or a STOP clause",
  "reading (owner, 2026-10-28, review m9)": "position under 0.3333 (1/3) FULL-REREAD (the second-tile re-reads come from DRAM, sigma 1 holds), over 0.6667 (2/3) L2-SERVED (served from L2), between MIXED; per cell, and per model on the median position over its readable cells. NOT READ when the sigma-1 and served prices are under 3 us or 10% of the sigma-1 price apart (a 3% price error, E1's rms bar, then moves position by at most 0.3, about one band); a model with no readable cell is NOT READ. A position below 0 or above 1 keeps its band and is reported as measured: the fit's own error enters position (the build review's synthetic kept-cell defect read 1.24)",
  "BYTES-D2": "the CAL ctl counter pages' second-tile cells: counted dram__bytes_read per GEMM against v4d's reads and the served reads, both computed on the laptop with A2's tile parameters (the page's own v4d_reads is an error on the wgmma T 128 cells, review m1; kept beside); share_not_seen = (v4d - counted) / (v4d - served)"
 },
